"notes":[
"Contests: from round 6, and every 7 rounds after, both teams race through the same objective: topple a Titan, hold two shrines, catch the gilded runners, or light three lanterns in the dark. The first team to finish gets a 90-second blessing and the full purse; the other gets half the gold if it finishes in time (Classic, Quick and their variants).",
"Mastery challenges: three tiers of three challenges per hero (Bronze, Silver, Gold). Each tier pays bonus mastery XP, and Gold gives that hero's own title. See them on hero select, the Profile and the Codex.",
"Smarter bots: area spells land on the biggest group of monsters, bots chase down a boss that got past them, and they play contests.",
"Match highlights: the end screen shows the best moments (big kill streaks, close calls, contests, boss kills, duels), each with a Watch button that opens the replay just before it."
]
}